    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the create-owner endpoint, keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (inherited by the response `Owner`/`OwnerDto` via `allOf`).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, since an owner may now supply its address structurally instead. The either-form rule is enforced in code.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner` model: added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (mapped to `address_line1`/`address_line2`) with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them by name in both directions.\n- Added the two nullable columns to all four DB schemas (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql). Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected.\n\n**Pipeline functions**\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress` (first create step): normalizes whichever address fields are supplied, prefers the structured form, and composes `address` = normalized `addressLine1` `+ \" \" + addressLine2` when `addressLine2` is present; falls back to the normalized flat `address` otherwise. Absent lines stay `null`.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields`: an owner is now valid when it has a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a flat `address`, plus `city`.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT path): now also carries `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`.\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation, and locality read `postcode`/`city` (shared structured fields), so they already resolve correctly \u2014 verified by the passing Cp10/Cp30 tests. The address-specific behavior is covered by Cp44 (normalize + compose + flat fallback), Cp12 (normalize structured line), and Cp01 (either-form validation).",
